<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link><description>World News Today: Read the latest world news headlines, Current International breaking news world wide. In depth analysis and top news headlines world wide.</description><language>en-gb</language><lastBuildDate>2026-08-26T14:00:47+05:30</lastBuildDate><atom:link type="application/rss+xml" rel="self" href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/rssfeeds/296589292.cms"/><copyright>Copyright:(C) Wed, 26 Aug 2026 14:00:47 IST Bennett Coleman &amp; Co. Ltd, http://in.indiatimes.com/policyterms/1554651.cms</copyright><docs>http://syndication.indiatimes.com/</docs><image><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><url>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/507610.cms</url><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link></image><item><title><![CDATA[How a family reunion in China ended in a 3-year prison term for artist Gao Zhen]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133533651.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Chinese artist Gao Zhen received a three-year prison sentence for his satirical artwork.  Authorities charged him with "infringing upon the reputation of heroes" for his art.  Gao's wife expressed deep disappointment and sadness over the unexpected conviction.  His supporters argue the artworks predate the law under which he was prosecuted.  The sentence highlights China's narrowing space for artistic and political expression.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/china/how-a-family-reunion-in-china-ended-in-a-3-year-prison-term-for-artist-gao-zhen/articleshow/133533651.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/china/how-a-family-reunion-in-china-ended-in-a-3-year-prison-term-for-artist-gao-zhen/articleshow/133533651.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-26T13:11:32+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vijaya Srivastava</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133533893,imgsize-224906.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Columbia engineers develop pigment-free coating that kept surfaces 6°C cooler under Arizona sun]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133532403.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Columbia Engineering researchers developed a porous polymer coating that can cool surfaces below the surrounding air temperature without using electricity. The coating replaces conventional white pigments with nano-to-microscale air voids that reflect sunlight and release heat towards the sky. Tests showed the surface stayed about 6°C below ambient temperature in Arizona and 3°C below it in Bangladesh.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/columbia-engineers-built-a-pigment-free-polymer-coating-filled-with-microscopic-air-pores-under-arizona-desert-sun-the-coated-surface-stayed-about-6c-below-ambient-air/articleshow/133532403.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/columbia-engineers-built-a-pigment-free-polymer-coating-filled-with-microscopic-air-pores-under-arizona-desert-sun-the-coated-surface-stayed-about-6c-below-ambient-air/articleshow/133532403.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-26T14:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133533395,imgsize-112714.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[47-year-old California pastor makes college football roster 30 years after an injury ended his career]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133533300.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/47-year-old-california-pastor-makes-college-football-roster-30-years-after-an-injury-ended-his-career-inspired-by-a-video-of-a-60-year-old-player/articleshow/133533300.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/47-year-old-california-pastor-makes-college-football-roster-30-years-after-an-injury-ended-his-career-inspired-by-a-video-of-a-60-year-old-player/articleshow/133533300.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-26T13:00:25+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133533550,imgsize-902969.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Nimaya Williams earns $40,000 BigFuture scholarship as one of only two students nationwide]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133532181.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Nimaya Williams has achieved a remarkable milestone by securing a $40,000 scholarship from College Board's BigFuture. This accolade was awarded to her for completing various college and career planning tasks available on their platform. The financial support alleviates a significant burden for her family regarding higher education costs, showcasing how strategic planning can create unforeseen pathways to success.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-nimaya-williams-the-north-carolina-junior-who-completed-free-college-planning-steps-and-became-one-of-only-two-students-nationwide-to-receive-a-40000-bigfuture-scholarship/articleshow/133532181.cms]]></link><guid><![C